WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.050
Good morning, Frau Kern. Today is the second day after your operation. This morning, we plan to sit you on the edge of the bed. How do you feel about that?

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:16.901
I would rather not. I feel dizzy today, and yesterday I felt a pulling pain when I stood up.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:38.165
Thank you for telling me. The dizziness is important, so we will not stand today. I would like to suggest an alternative: first I will measure your blood pressure while you are lying down. If you agree, we will then sit you only on the edge of the bed, without standing. Would that be all right?

00:00:38.165 --> 00:00:41.169
And what if I feel dizzy again while sitting?

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:55.797
Then we will lay you straight back down, as required after your operation, and I will stay with you. Tell me as soon as it starts; you do not need to wait until it becomes severe.

00:00:55.797 --> 00:00:59.872
All right, I agree. Let us try sitting, then.

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:13.796
Frau Kern, your blood pressure while sitting has fallen to 98/60, and the dizziness is still present. We will stop here. I will inform the doctor, and we will try again later.

00:01:13.796 --> 00:01:24.558
Dr Weber, this is Amina Saleh from the surgical ward. I am calling about Frau Kern in room 12, on the second day after a right total hip replacement.

00:01:24.558 --> 00:01:26.178
Yes, what is the matter with her?

00:01:26.178 --> 00:01:44.098
During the planned mobilisation she reported dizziness. Her blood pressure was 128/76 lying down and 98/60 sitting; pulse 96. I stopped the mobilisation and laid her back down according to the postoperative instructions.
